  "body": "Found in the second safety read of PR #3058 (#1883). Refs #1882, #1885.\n\n**Now (with PR #3058):**\n- The operation has no standoff height. The cut plane is the top of the sheet (`crates/app/src/operation/waterjet_op.rs:96`, `cut_z = top`). Plasma has `cut_height`.\n- The CL has no jet on/off record and no pierce dwell record. Travel moves are rapids at the clearance plane; lit moves are feeds. The pierce dwell and the abrasive delay are in the path notes only.\n- No shipped post serves `Kind::Waterjet`. But a user script can declare `serves = [\"waterjet\"]` (`posting_serves/tests.rs:9`). That script gets this CL: no jet on/off, no dwell, and the nozzle tip on the sheet for a machine with a Z axis.\n\n**Risk:** a nozzle that touches the sheet, or a jet that is not switched, on a machine that runs a user post. No shipped post can do it.\n\n**Wanted (one of the two, the first is smaller):**\n1. The post gate refuses a waterjet operation by name until the jet records (#1882) and the waterjet laws (#1885) are in. The refusal says what is missing.\n2. Or: add the standoff height to the operation (validated above the sheet top) and the jet on/off and dwell records to the CL.\n\n**Also:**\n- The stock simulation skips Probe, Torch and Wire, but not Waterjet (`stock_sim.rs:288`). The nozzle goes into the dexel simulation as a cutter at the sheet top. `verify` gives no visible \"not judged\" note for a waterjet operation. A kind that no law judges must say so.\n- Corner slow-down, taper and kerf lag are not modelled. Say so in the path notes or in the decision file.\n- With a lead-in of 0 the pierce is on the kerf ring at the edge of the part, and no note says so.\n- The label \"In control (G41/G42)\" uses G-code words (the plasma page has the same label). The row label \"Tab position\" is there two times (`waterjet_page.rs:110`).\n",
